# Version control and local configuration
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*

# Python environments, caches, builds, and test output
.venv
venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.eggs
build
dist
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage*
htmlcov

# Development-only files and runtime output
# NEVER exclude a digest input. The digest set is stated ONCE, in
# scripts/quality_receipt.py (DIGEST_DIRECTORIES and DIGEST_FILES); it is not
# restated here. tests/ and scripts/ are in it, so they ARE needed in the build
# context even though only the "quality-receipt" stage copies them. Excluding one
# does not fail loudly: the gate stage recomputes a digest over fewer files and
# reports "the tree does not match its receipt", which reads like a stale receipt
# and is not one. tests/lane_config/test_image_plumbing.py fails instead when any
# pattern below would drop a digest input from the context.
*.log
logs
*.pid
.cache
.agri-local-runs
tmp
docker-compose.yml
Makefile
